  <Patch Id="VM4tBf8TDXWp9JGtzqpV4f">
    <Canvas Id="OiAyR1KRRHXKmt2dWrZGfs" DefaultCategory="Main" BordersChecked="false" CanvasType="FullCategory" />
    <!--

    ************************ Application ************************

-->
    <Node Name="Application" Bounds="100,180" Id="NJh3D4J1gfolEb7Po36rjj">
      <p:NodeReference>
        <Choice Kind="ContainerDefinition" Name="Process" />
        <CategoryReference Kind="Category" Name="Primitive" />
      </p:NodeReference>
      <Patch Id="Dn4LeMcAMCfNfobfVBTRfU">
        <Canvas Id="bAfdzL0v94dqcC5PrhM2Gh" CanvasType="Group">
          <Pad Id="Hsg2biaLqCOVWEKxQQrucB" Bounds="85,16,555,52" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="How To Write a ShaderEffect">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">25</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="q0MQbJhwYBlga7aqN9GVeO" Bounds="85,85,572,133" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="ShaderEffect [Qt]&#xD;&#xA;- Input: element the shader reads as sampler2D &quot;source&quot;, unconnected = generative&#xD;&#xA;- Fragment Code: GLSL text in the patch (default is a commented template)&#xD;&#xA;- Fragment Shader: Path to a baked .qsb, or builtin:wave&#xD;&#xA;- Uniforms: spread of nodes from Qt.Elements.Uniform&#xD;&#xA;- Auto Size (default on)">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="GT7uBkJDVdVgrgRVXuTFjj" Bounds="85,1239,1387,277" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Notes:&#xD;&#xA;- The Input is not drawn itself, only the effect output is. Bounds, Transform and Opacity belong on the ShaderEffect, not on its Input; Auto Size takes the size of the Input.&#xD;&#xA;- Fragment Code is baked in the background while you edit; if it has an error, the last working version keeps drawing. It needs no tools: VL.Qt bakes the text itself (Qt Shader Tools).&#xD;&#xA;- Fragment Shader wins over Fragment Code if set. A broken path draws nothing. Vertex Code / Vertex Shader (optional pins) work the same way.&#xD;&#xA;- Uniforms: values by name from the nodes in Qt.Elements.Uniform (Float, Int, Bool, Vector2/3/4, Color, Matrix, Texture, Image), collected in a spread.&#xD;&#xA;- A GLSL error with its line number, a missing file, a broken .qsb or an unknown / wrongly typed uniform shows at the node and in the log.&#xD;&#xA;- Shader language is GLSL 440, baked with Qt's qsb tool (Qt host tools, not part of VL.Qt): qsb --glsl &quot;100es,120,150&quot; --hlsl 50 --msl 12 -o x.frag.qsb x.frag. qsb is only needed for shaders you bake yourself or ship precompiled.&#xD;&#xA;- Uniform block: layout(std140, binding = 0), qt_Matrix (mat4) and qt_Opacity (float) first, then your members. Member names must match the Uniform node names (case sensitive).&#xD;&#xA;- The Input is layout(binding = 1) uniform sampler2D source; texture coordinates come in as qt_TexCoord0, the result goes to vec4 fragColor (location 0).&#xD;&#xA;- The Input is premultiplied, so the output must be premultiplied too (rgb * alpha). Color uniforms arrive premultiplied as well (rgb * a); Vector4 is passed unchanged.&#xD;&#xA;- shaders/tint.frag next to this patch is the source of the tint example, shaders/tint.frag.qsb is the baked file the node loads.&#xD;&#xA;- builtin:wave needs an Input (uniforms time, amplitude, frequency).&#xD;&#xA;- Shader files in a qtshaders folder next to the patch become nodes with their own pins, no Uniform nodes needed: see HowTo Create Shader Nodes from Files.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="l1SD6nTqokP2TameZsMO4k" Bounds="100,288,480,46" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="1  builtin:wave on a Text: an LFO drives time (a Motion demo). Amplitude and frequency sit in the Float nodes.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="YULeqdV6FtmduvfWj96B29" Bounds="620,288,480,46" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="2  Your own shader: shaders/tint.frag.qsb with a Color and a Float uniform on a Rectangle.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
